@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] pr-lifecycle-is-visible
The pull request detail header MUST visibly say Merged or Closed when GitHub reports
that lifecycle, using the app's existing state ink and glyphs independently of check
results. A merge timestamp or an observed merged state MUST take precedence over an
open, closed or draft copy and MUST disable merge actions; a fresh known open overview
MAY replace a previously closed copy after reopening. Missing or unrecognized lifecycle
without terminal evidence MUST NOT be treated as open. A current diff's known state MUST
replace a cached overview's older state; lifecycle and same-PR link refreshes MUST update
the displayed status without a manual Refresh. A known lifecycle from the list MUST
survive the opening preview (Tavi, 20 Oct 2026: "On PRs that have already been merged,
we have no indication that they've been merged").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product;security] shared-overview-requires-real-host-services
Both hosts MUST render the same production Overview, Conversation, metadata and reading
sheets. Clipboard, external GitHub/browser destinations and lifecycle MUST use the one
required native actions service. Inline-edit Back MUST cancel the field before the
shared route pops, through the host's existing Back dispatcher; iOS MUST NOT install a
second competing edge recognizer. A host without that dispatcher MUST keep text editing
unavailable even when the server grants permission. Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026
shared Overview and native-service plan, preserving pr-edit-in-place and pr-number-opens-github.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture;security] shared-overview-capabilities-precede-ai-actions
A host MUST declare unavailable AI reading, setup and paid actions before exposing
Overview controls or issuing their requests. Supported AI content MUST use the actual
production renderer with citations, task guards and complete outcomes; an empty or
no-op content provider MUST NOT claim support. Android MUST retain its current Brief,
AI summary, file note and findings behavior through the same common implementations.
A host without verified native rendering and citation routes MUST say that kept AI
results are unavailable and MUST NOT start invisible work. Source: the accepted
21 Oct 2026 ordered extraction, explicit OverviewAiContent decision and subsequent
authorization to share the actual AI reading renderers and native SVG adapter.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] shared-overview-commit-days-use-local-calendar
Commit-day groups MUST retain their existing contiguous order and Today, Yesterday,
English weekday/date labels in the device's time zone. A missing commit date MUST
follow the preceding group or read Undated when first. Android MUST retain its current
java.time formatter; native calendar adaptation MUST NOT change the commit indices or
selection behavior. Source: existing CommitsSheet/commitDays behavior retained by
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] shared-code-pinch-reflows-and-keeps-the-line
A two-finger code pinch MUST resize the existing font and line height and ease layout
at most once per frame. When the diff supplies its optional PinchKeeper, the line
under the starting pivot MUST stay there. Finger changes
MUST NOT jerk or pan the code, one finger MUST keep scrolling the list, and the final
bounded size MUST be saved once on release. Source: existing CodeView behavior, M9,
L17 and O21, preserved by Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS decision; DESIGN.md rule 93.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-file-sheet-focus-belongs-to-its-view
The existing changed and unchanged file sheets MUST use the same shared diff rows,
line-focus positioning, left-edge reset and mark timer. A stale file/view MUST NOT
consume a newer focus or move its viewport after suspension; a full revision change
MUST restart the sheet's file/highlight work even when the path and text are unchanged.
Source: existing diff-focus-lands-whole and tour-code-opens-in-a-sheet, N20/N21/L28,
preserved by Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 shared session/source ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-thread-actions-belong-to-the-route
A thread card MUST issue at most one write at a time and keep rejected writes recoverable
on that card. After route or account cancellation, a late response MUST NOT clear a
draft, reload another route, show an error, or play completion feedback. Source: existing
ThreadActions write policy and Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 shared session/source ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-diff-reads-belong-to-the-view
Full-file contents, syntax tokens, expanded gaps and line drafts MUST belong to the
session's current source, key, head and view revision. An earlier read MUST NOT refill
or overwrite a newer view, even when the transport completes after cancellation.
Highlight requests MUST keep the existing 400-line limit and missing-row retry policy.
Source: existing diff-highlight-respects-server-batches and Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 shared
session/source ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;product] shared-file-diff-retains-its-rows-and-annotations
Both hosts MUST use the existing full-bleed unified/split diff rows, exact palette and
word emphasis, gap and full-file behavior, gutters, selection/drag targets and thread
card placement. AI results MUST use the actual shared annotation renderer for notes, findings and asks;
a host without complete result support MUST suppress those results through the single
host capability policy, never substitute an empty renderer. Tavi's 21 Oct extraction now
shares the saved Ask forms and the complete annotation renderer with the diff. Source: existing
FileDiff.kt and diff contracts, DESIGN.md rules 49, 92 and 94, preserved by Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-line-input-belongs-to-the-drawn-file
Line taps, long presses, gutter positions and drag completion/cancellation MUST only
mutate the exact file and full view which drew those handlers. Retired callbacks,
including a head A to B to A transition, MUST NOT create or clear a newer selection,
draft or line-action sheet. Pinch and focus callbacks MUST reject a retired file even
when its path matches. Source: existing diff line-selection behavior and Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 shared session/source ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-diff-comments-keep-the-drawn-target
The diff comment field MUST retain the existing pending-review mode, selected side,
range and drawn head commit. Both host readiness and the session's server write
permission MUST precede the request. One send MUST run at a time; rejected sends MUST
remain retryable. A retired field or late write MUST NOT clear a newer input, reload
another view or publish its feedback. Source: existing DiffBar comment behavior,
DESIGN.md rule 94 and Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 shared session/source ownership plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;product;security] shared-diff-screen-keeps-the-original-file-journey
The shared Diff screen MUST retain the original side-by-side file motion, code-first
horizontal scrolling, pinned counts, comment bar, line actions and per-file scroll
positions. Every retained navigation, Ask, clipboard, comment or viewer-progress
handler MUST belong to its drawn full review revision and exact file. Delayed Reviewed
auto-advance MUST NOT move a replacement view or a reader who has moved to another
file. Hosts MUST suppress unavailable writes, Ask and viewer-progress controls before
work; viewer progress MUST NOT require GitHub comment permission. Android Full MUST
retain its existing comment and Reviewed workflows. Source: existing PrDiffScreen.kt,
DESIGN.md rules 40, 42, 90, 92, 94, 105 and 107, and Tavi's 21 Oct shared iOS plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-thread-writes-require-current-host-readiness
Reply, Resolve and the viewer's comment edit/delete controls MUST require both the
current canonical canWriteComments host policy and the server's write permission.
Retained callbacks MUST recheck those permissions and their captured session/view
before sending. A disposed or retired thread's late response MUST NOT clear a draft,
reload reviews or publish feedback/error in its replacement. Unsent reply/edit state
MUST belong to its session, full view and thread. Android Full MUST retain the existing
requests and busy/retry behavior. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct shared iOS readiness and source
isolation plan, preserving existing review thread ownership and permissions.

